--- !u!114 &8574102048107967245
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 5660449419154731507}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Not all Jo\u0308tunn are made equal. Not all Stories end with the last
    chapter. Some, few indeed, but still some stories travel forward, cut from time,
    from the mind of man, until they reappear in our minds, our lives, and they bring
    change.\n\nRagnarok has ended. The end of time, the world and all that is known
    to men and god destroyed. As it was written and foretold from the beginning of
    all that was known.. But like all prophecies not everything was as expected..
    Ragnarok the death of the gods, the cataclysm that destroyed the realms was not
    an ending. It was the beginning and the cycle began anew.\n\nIn the icy realm
    of Niflheim, where frost clung to the very air and snow whispered secrets of
    old, there was born a giant, a being of ice and cold, born of a lineage shrouded
    in mystery. This giant, unlike his brethren of war and strife, bore within him
    a spark of creation, a flame that burned brighter than the bitter winds of his
    homeland. The last gift of the builder and his trusted companion Sva\xF0ilfari,
    sent to his aid after his death by the hand of Thor, son of Odin.\n\nAs the ages
    passed and Ragnarok swept the realms in its cataclysmic embrace, this young giant
    wandered the frozen expanse, his heart heavy with solitude amidst the ruins of
    gods and worlds. Yet, in his solitude, he found solace in the whispers of the
    wind and the silent wisdom of the ancient ice.\nOne day, as the echoes of Ragnarok
    faded into the past, the giant felt a stirring within him, a longing for adventure
    and purpose beyond the desolation of Niflheim. Heeding the call of the unknown,
    he embarked on a journey through the newly formed realms, each one a tapestry
    woven with wonders and marvels he had never dared to dream.\nIn his travels,
    the giant encountered civilizations teeming with life, from the ethereal forests
    of Alfheim to the bustling cities of Midgard. Along the way, he unearthed remnants
    of forgotten magic, echoes of a time when gods and mortals walked side by side.\n\nDrawn
    to the mysteries of magic like a moth to a flame, the giant delved deep into
    his own abilities, unlocking hidden talents and ancient powers passed down from
    his forebears. With each revelation, he felt the weight of destiny upon his broad
    shoulders, a legacy beckoning him to rise above the ashes of destruction and
    forge a new path.\n\nInspired by the beauty and creativity of the realms, the
    giant resolved to wield his powers not as a weapon of war, but as a beacon of
    hope and enlightenment. In the heart of Niflheim, he raised a citadel of ice
    and crystal, a sanctuary where scholars and mages from across the realms could
    gather in harmony and unity.\nLore\nWithin the walls of his citadel, the giant
    fostered a spirit of cooperation and understanding, as beings of all races and
    creeds came together to study the mysteries of magic and the wonders of the cosmos.
    Together, they sought to unlock the full potential of their abilities, forging
    bonds that transcended the boundaries of time and space.\n\nBut the giant's quest
    did not end there. Armed with knowledge and wisdom, he ventured forth into the
    far reaches of the realms, bringing light to the darkest corners and solace to
    the weary souls he encountered. Wherever he went, he left behind a legacy of
    peace and enlightenment, a testament to the power of compassion and unity in
    a world scarred by strife.\n\nAnd so, the young giant embraced his destiny with
    a fierce determination, knowing that in his hands lay the power to shape a new
    era of prosperity and understanding for all who dwelled in the realms. And though
    the road ahead was fraught with challenges and trials, he faced it with courage
    and conviction, a true champion of creation and enlightenment in a world reborn
    from the ashes of Ragnarok."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 81cc66dda6eef5e4d9c0a1dec8c47766, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 4928202655278997800, guid: 81cc66dda6eef5e4d9c0a1dec8c47766, type: 2}
